From: Satoshi Nakamoto <satoshi@MacBook-Pro.local>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 08:43:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(browse): scope console and network logs to the pinned
 tab

Commands pinned to a tab (BROWSE_TAB / --tab-id) now read and clear only
that tab's console and network entries, so parallel clients driving
separate tabs don't see each other's logs. Entries carry their tab id and
a sequence number; a tab-scoped clear records a cursor instead of emptying
the shared buffer. Response and size matching also require the same tab.
Unpinned commands keep the global view.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
